Evidence class (rule 10): measure
What would vindicate the flat model (rule 5): Io's eclipses keeping time with no delay that follows
  the Earth-Jupiter distance (Io's clock alone fitting as well as the light time), or a delay whose
  free curve does not land on the numbers one astronomical unit predicts (its swing over the synodic
  cycle, its second harmonic and its change with Jupiter's distance from the Sun).
