Notes: Only Io (satellite 1) is fitted. The raw file is used, not the standard file whose O-C come
  from a satellite theory. Lieske reduced local apparent times to UT with each site's longitude,
  which he sometimes corrected from the residuals of an ephemeris (the 1983 paper, Hoai-Ngan); a
  wrong longitude shifts a site's timings by a constant, and every site with 30 timings or more gets
  its own free offset in each era, so no such correction can reach the light time. The DE440 variant
  (data/moon/eclcraters/raw/de440.bsp, fog fetch moon-eclcraters) is a check of the orbits' shape;
  without that file it is skipped. Method and references: go doc -all ./internal/build/romer.

Written by `fog build explain` from data/sun/romer/dataset.json and data/sun/romer/inputs.lock: edit those, not this file.
